WEBVTT

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:06.635
Personal Log, Stardate 48546.2.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.937
Our journey home
is several weeks old now,

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:12.570
and I have begun to notice
in my crew, and in myself,

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:15.979
a subtle change as the reality
of our situation settles in.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:18.107
Here in the Delta Quadrant,

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.949
we are virtually
the entire family of man.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.581
We are more than a crew,
and I must find a way

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.386
to be more than a Captain
to these people...

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:28.883
but it's not clear to me
exactly how to begin.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.490
At the Academy, we're taught
that a Captain is expected

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.467
to maintain a certain distance.

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:37.766
Until now, I have
always been comfortable

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:38.930
with that distance.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:43.532
Captain, I...

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.567
I didn't realize there was
an inspection scheduled.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.239
Not an inspection, Lieutenant.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.713
A stroll.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.876
We should have the warp drive
up and running by 0900 hours.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.715
Recalibrating
the reactant injectors

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.516
is the only thing
we have left to do.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.250
Carry on.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.850
Maybe this is
just the way it works.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.088
Maybe the distance
is necessary.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.493
Maybe more than ever now,

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.464
they need me
to be larger than life.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:09.332
I only wish
I felt larger than life.

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:11.360
Computer, delete last sentence.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.607
Gentlemen.

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:18.110
As you were.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.203
So, has Neelix concocted

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.804
anything interesting
this morning?

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:25.375
There's an ancient
Chinese curse, Captain...

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.579
"May you live
in interesting times."

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.281
Mealtime is always interesting

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:31.256
now that Neelix
is in the kitchen.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.986
We shouldn't judge him
too harshly.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.391
He is helping us
conserve replicator energy.

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.395
And I'm sure

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.363
the gastrointestinal
problems will go away,

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:41.162
as soon as our systems
get used to his, uh...

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:42.691
gourmet touch.

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:48.103
Well, see you at duty call.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.370
We should have
asked her to join us.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:58.009
Ensigns don't invite
Captains to sit down.

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:59.676
Why not?

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.244
Because they don't.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.516
Well, what's wrong with
showing a little courtesy?

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.048
Captains don't want courtesy.

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.651
They want respect.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:11.027
That's why they don't get chummy
with the lower ranks.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:16.296
Well, who else is she supposed
to get chummy with out here?

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.133
There aren't many other
Captains and Admirals

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:19.195
for her to talk to.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:20.831
If she wants to sit with us,

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:22.501
she'll ask us to join her.

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.339
That's the way it's done.

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:28.871
I think you're working
from an old rule book, Paris.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.383
Neelix?

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.407
Captain!

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:07.853
May I say,
you look beautiful this morning.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.878
Is that a new color lipstick?

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:13.256
No, no, it's the same color
I always wear.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.954
Well, perhaps
it's just the way the glow

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.962
of the food heater lamps
hits you,

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.429
but you look wonderful.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.829
Not to suggest

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.060
you don't always look wonderful.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.399
Neelix, do we have
any coffee left?

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:27.065
No, but we have
something even better.

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:29.973
I don't want something
even better, I want coffee.

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:31.510
It's made from
a proteinaceous seed

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.806
I discovered on an expedition...

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:33.971
Never mind.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.071
I'll use one of my replicator
rations for coffee.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:38.606
That would not be appropriate,
Captain.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.314
I beg your pardon?

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.384
You need to set
an example for the crew.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:52.558
Well, thank you
for reminding me.

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:53.827
You're welcome.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.834
After all, if you want the crew

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.733
to begin to accept
natural food alternatives

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.568
instead of further depleting
our energy reserves,

00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:04.941
you need to encourage them
by your own choices, don't you?

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:09.743
Fine. Give me your even-better-
than-coffee substitute.

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.909
And how about some
Takar loggerhead eggs

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.213
with that this morning?

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.278
Just... coffee.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:18.654
It's a tiny bit richer blend
than you're used to,

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.352
but you'll learn to love it.

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:21.724
Bridge to Janeway.

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.490
On my way. Janeway out.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.225
Tomorrow maybe.

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:35.741
Ah.

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:37.072
Yes, Commander?

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.407
There was no need

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:39.741
for you to come to the Bridge,
Captain.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:40.837
Yes, there was.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.472
I just wanted to alert
you to a nebula

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.107
we've picked up
on long-range sensors.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.345
Put it on screen.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:49.287
Magnify.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:51.222
There are unusually high levels

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.657
of omicron particles
within this nebula, Captain.

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:56.423
Are you thinking we could
collect these omicron particles

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:59.431
to provide an additional
antimatter reserve, Lieutenant?

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:00.989
Precisely.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.126
Senior Bridge Officers,
report for duty.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.730
Commander, set a new course.

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:09.674
There's coffee in that nebula.

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:03.412
Exploring this nebula
should raise some spirits

00:07:03.456 --> 00:07:05.390
around here, don't you think,
Commander?

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:07.154
No way to go but up.

00:07:07.193 --> 00:07:10.390
You're closer
to the crew than I am.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.364
How bad is it?

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.691
There's a nuanka...
a period of mourning

00:07:16.736 --> 00:07:18.260
that everyone's going through.

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:19.396
It's a natural reaction.

00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:21.566
I'm worried about them.

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:23.939
I wish we had
a Counselor on board,

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:26.274
but the nature of our mission
didn't require one.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.275
We talk to animals.

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:33.183
It's a Native American
tradition.

00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:34.413
Animals?

00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:35.853
Our own counselors.

00:07:35.888 --> 00:07:37.480
We're taught
that an animal guide

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:39.286
accompanies us through life.

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:41.725
Basically, it's what Carl
Jung thought he invented

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:42.785
when he came up with

00:07:42.829 --> 00:07:45.730
his "active imagination"
technique in 1932,

00:07:45.765 --> 00:07:46.732
but we'd been doing

00:07:46.766 --> 00:07:48.734
pretty much the same
thing for centuries.

00:07:48.768 --> 00:07:51.259
Is there a different
animal guide for everyone?

00:07:51.304 --> 00:07:52.498
Actually, yes.

00:07:52.538 --> 00:07:53.505
Let me guess.

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:55.837
Yours is a bear.

00:07:57.543 --> 00:07:58.771
Why do you say that?

00:07:58.811 --> 00:08:01.609
You strike me as the bear type.

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:02.875
Thank you.

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:04.348
The bear is
a very powerful animal.

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:06.044
It has great pokattah,

00:08:06.085 --> 00:08:08.417
but he's not my animal guide.

00:08:08.454 --> 00:08:11.423
The creature that guides us
doesn't define who we are.

00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:13.258
It merely chooses to be with us.

00:08:13.391 --> 00:08:16.326
Okay. If not a bear,
then what?

00:08:16.361 --> 00:08:18.420
I can't tell you that.

00:08:18.463 --> 00:08:21.193
It would offend my animal guide
if I spoke its name.

00:08:21.232 --> 00:08:23.496
But he guides you well?

00:08:23.534 --> 00:08:25.229
Actually, it's female.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:28.364
But yes, she usually
guides me very well.

00:08:28.406 --> 00:08:30.931
Can one just choose
her own animal guide?

00:08:31.042 --> 00:08:32.509
It's not quite that simple.

00:08:32.543 --> 00:08:33.737
Captain,

00:08:33.778 --> 00:08:35.939
we are approaching
the perimeter of the nebula.

00:08:36.014 --> 00:08:37.709
Slow to one-third impulse.

00:08:37.749 --> 00:08:40.877
If you're interested,
I'll be glad to teach you

00:08:40.918 --> 00:08:42.749
how to contact
your animal guide.

00:08:42.787 --> 00:08:44.618
You've got a date.

00:08:44.656 --> 00:08:46.556
Analysis, Mr. Kim.

00:08:46.591 --> 00:08:48.320
Seven AU's in diameter.

00:08:48.359 --> 00:08:50.554
Sensors are picking up
intermittent gamma

00:08:50.595 --> 00:08:51.926
and thermal emissions.

00:08:51.963 --> 00:08:53.931
Nothing our shields
can't handle.

00:08:53.965 --> 00:08:56.456
Mr. Paris, any problems
for navigation?

00:08:56.501 --> 00:08:59.061
I'm showing
mostly hydrogen, helium,

00:08:59.103 --> 00:09:00.627
and hydroxyl radicals.

00:09:00.672 --> 00:09:02.469
Some local dust nodules.

00:09:02.507 --> 00:09:04.372
I don't see them
giving us any trouble.

00:09:04.409 --> 00:09:06.536
Mr. Tuvok, can you find us

00:09:06.577 --> 00:09:09.341
a rich deposit of omicron
particles in there?

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.712
A significant concentration
appears to exist

00:09:11.749 --> 00:09:13.774
approximately
64 million kilometers

00:09:13.818 --> 00:09:15.115
inside the perimeter.

00:09:15.153 --> 00:09:16.245
Set coordinates.

00:09:16.287 --> 00:09:17.413
Aye, Captain.

00:09:17.455 --> 00:09:18.820
Engines at one-quarter impulse.

00:09:18.856 --> 00:09:20.619
Engage.

00:09:28.166 --> 00:09:30.361
I've never seen
anything like it.

00:09:30.401 --> 00:09:33.234
Tuvok to Kim.

00:09:33.271 --> 00:09:35.739
Mr. Kim, that is a comment

00:09:35.773 --> 00:09:36.899
we would prefer not to hear

00:09:36.941 --> 00:09:39.068
from a Senior Officer
on the Bridge.

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:41.738
It makes the Junior
Officers nervous.

00:09:41.779 --> 00:09:43.303
Yes, sir.

00:09:45.283 --> 00:09:47.649
Density has increased
to 42 percent.

00:09:47.685 --> 00:09:48.777
Cause?

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:50.151
Not sure.

00:09:50.188 --> 00:09:51.246
We seem to be drawing

00:09:51.289 --> 00:09:53.519
some interstellar dust
toward us.

00:09:53.558 --> 00:09:55.423
Engineering, could
the magnetic field

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:57.951
from our impulse engines
be attracting this dust?

00:09:57.995 --> 00:09:59.656
It's a good possibility,
Captain.

00:10:01.299 --> 00:10:04.962
I'm showing the dust with
a return force ratio of 4.1.

00:10:05.069 --> 00:10:06.969
Recommend we shut down impulse
and go to thrusters.

00:10:07.071 --> 00:10:07.969
Acknowledged.

00:10:08.072 --> 00:10:09.198
Engage thrusters.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:10.832
Ahead slow.

00:10:10.875 --> 00:10:13.435
Density still increasing.

00:10:13.478 --> 00:10:15.207
Up by 70 percent now.

00:10:15.246 --> 00:10:16.213
Mr. Tuvok?

00:10:16.247 --> 00:10:17.441
The level of resistance

00:10:17.482 --> 00:10:19.416
poses no danger to the hull
at this time, Captain.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.884
How far to your omicron
particle deposits?

00:10:21.919 --> 00:10:23.978
12,400 kilometers.

00:10:24.021 --> 00:10:25.079
Maintain course and...

00:10:25.123 --> 00:10:26.954
Report!

00:10:28.192 --> 00:10:29.989
We're at a dead stop now.

00:10:30.094 --> 00:10:31.493
Shutting down thrusters.

00:10:31.529 --> 00:10:34.157
We seem to have encountered
an energy barrier.

00:10:34.198 --> 00:10:35.995
Is it natural or artificial?

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:38.261
We're not reading
any directed energy source

00:10:38.302 --> 00:10:39.269
down here, Captain.

00:10:39.303 --> 00:10:41.430
My guess is
it's a natural phenomenon.

00:10:41.472 --> 00:10:43.406
How far are we
from the particles, Lieutenant?

00:10:43.441 --> 00:10:45.466
Just over 7,000 kilometers.

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:47.444
It's conceivable
this energy barrier

00:10:47.478 --> 00:10:50.003
is related to those particles.

00:10:50.081 --> 00:10:52.413
Mr. Kim, if you could get
a transporter beam

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:53.417
through the barrier...

00:10:53.451 --> 00:10:54.418
Can't do it, Captain.

00:10:54.452 --> 00:10:55.612
The thoron emissions
of the barrier

00:10:55.653 --> 00:10:57.120
would interfere with
the transporter signal.

00:10:57.155 --> 00:10:58.520
Ms. Torres,
do we have enough power

00:10:58.556 --> 00:11:00.023
to take the ship
through the barrier?

00:11:00.057 --> 00:11:03.652
The barrier appears
to be only 50 meters deep.

00:11:03.694 --> 00:11:04.661
A four-second burst

00:11:04.695 --> 00:11:06.253
at maximum thrusters
ought to do it.

00:11:06.297 --> 00:11:07.730
All right.

00:11:07.765 --> 00:11:08.789
Maximum shields.

00:11:08.833 --> 00:11:10.460
Engage full thrusters
for four seconds

00:11:10.501 --> 00:11:11.729
and then drop to one-quarter.

00:11:11.769 --> 00:11:13.862
Acknowledged.
Engaging thrusters.

00:11:19.777 --> 00:11:21.938
What do you make of it,
Mr. Tuvok?

00:11:21.979 --> 00:11:25.346
I am unable to offer
an identification, Captain.

00:11:27.318 --> 00:11:28.945
Kim to Tuvok.

00:11:28.986 --> 00:11:30.886
In other words,

00:11:30.922 --> 00:11:32.913
you've never seen
anything like it?

00:11:32.957 --> 00:11:35.118
Oh, I promise
not to tell the Junior Officers.

00:11:38.763 --> 00:11:39.923
Captain,

00:11:39.964 --> 00:11:42.728
the breach we just made,
where we penetrated the field...

00:11:42.767 --> 00:11:44.962
it just closed behind us.

00:11:48.139 --> 00:11:49.766
Kes!

00:11:49.807 --> 00:11:52.935
Oh! Now look
what she's gotten us into!

00:11:52.977 --> 00:11:55.844
Do all nebulas look like that?

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:56.972
I wouldn't know.

00:11:57.014 --> 00:11:58.811
I'm smart enough
to go around nebulas

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:00.112
when I encounter them.

00:12:00.151 --> 00:12:04.087
These people are
natural-born explorers, Neelix.

00:12:04.121 --> 00:12:08.080
These people are natural-born
idiots if you ask me.

00:12:08.125 --> 00:12:11.117
They don't appreciate
what they have here.

00:12:11.162 --> 00:12:12.652
This ship
is the match of any vessel

00:12:12.697 --> 00:12:15.257
within a hundred light years,
and what do they do with it?

00:12:15.299 --> 00:12:16.891
"Well, let's see
if we can't find

00:12:16.934 --> 00:12:19.061
"some space anomaly today
that might

00:12:19.103 --> 00:12:20.297
rip it apart!"

00:12:20.338 --> 00:12:23.102
I don't think
the Captain is an idiot.

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:25.301
She cares a great deal
about her crew.

00:12:25.343 --> 00:12:27.834
You don't care a great deal
about your crew

00:12:27.879 --> 00:12:29.574
and introduce them
to the specter of death

00:12:29.614 --> 00:12:30.842
at every opportunity.

00:12:30.882 --> 00:12:33.476
And I speak as a member
of that crew now.

00:12:33.518 --> 00:12:35.315
I'm not sure I would have
wanted you to come along

00:12:35.353 --> 00:12:36.615
had I known
that this is what we...

00:12:36.654 --> 00:12:38.281
I think it's wonderful.

00:12:38.322 --> 00:12:39.846
Wonderful?

00:12:39.891 --> 00:12:40.858
If I were Captain,

00:12:40.892 --> 00:12:42.325
I'd open every crack
in the universe

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.988
and peek inside,
just like Captain Janeway does.

00:12:45.096 --> 00:12:48.532
I don't deny the romantic...

00:12:48.566 --> 00:12:50.932
quality of this sort
of... casting about.

00:12:50.968 --> 00:12:53.129
I wouldn't exactly
call it wonderful.

00:13:03.147 --> 00:13:04.774
Although...

00:13:04.815 --> 00:13:08.478
it's getting more
wonderful by the minute.

00:13:08.519 --> 00:13:12.182
I've never kissed anyone
inside a nebula before.

00:13:14.759 --> 00:13:17.284
What did I tell you?

00:13:17.328 --> 00:13:18.727
Red Alert.

00:13:18.763 --> 00:13:19.730
Whatever they are,

00:13:19.764 --> 00:13:20.958
they're passing right
through our shields.

00:13:21.032 --> 00:13:22.966
Try reversing
the shield polarity.

00:13:23.067 --> 00:13:23.965
Mr. Tuvok?

00:13:24.068 --> 00:13:25.057
They appear to be made up

00:13:25.102 --> 00:13:26.501
of a non-reactive
material that our sensors

00:13:26.537 --> 00:13:27.629
do not recognize, Captain.

00:13:27.672 --> 00:13:28.730
Clarify
Are we under attack?

00:13:28.773 --> 00:13:29.967
Uncertain.

00:13:30.041 --> 00:13:31.599
There is no indication
of directed fire.

00:13:31.642 --> 00:13:32.609
Torres to Bridge.

00:13:32.643 --> 00:13:33.610
Go ahead.

00:13:33.644 --> 00:13:35.407
These things
are sticking to the hull.

00:13:35.446 --> 00:13:37.744
And I'm showing a drain
on our energy reserves.

00:13:37.782 --> 00:13:40.342
A drain?
Why would we be losing energy?

00:13:40.384 --> 00:13:41.749
I'm not sure, Captain.

00:13:41.786 --> 00:13:42.753
They seem to be drawing it

00:13:42.787 --> 00:13:44.277
right through the shield grid
along the hull.

00:13:44.322 --> 00:13:45.949
We've lost five percent
of our energy reserves.

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:47.855
Recommend we shut down
all non-essential systems.

00:13:47.892 --> 00:13:48.984
Do it.

00:13:49.026 --> 00:13:51.688
Reversing shield polarity
hasn't had any effect.

00:13:51.729 --> 00:13:53.424
Energy reserves
are down eight percent.

00:13:53.464 --> 00:13:55.364
This is not what I had in mind.

00:13:55.399 --> 00:13:57.890
Mr. Paris, take us back
through the energy barrier

00:13:57.935 --> 00:13:58.993
and out of here.

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:00.128
Reversing course.

00:14:00.171 --> 00:14:01.138
Full thrusters.

00:14:01.172 --> 00:14:03.003
Thrusters firing.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:15.476
We're not penetrating
the energy barrier this time.

00:14:15.519 --> 00:14:17.749
Sensors show a buildup
of magneside dust

00:14:17.788 --> 00:14:18.948
along the outer rim
of the barrier.

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:20.756
Engineering, I need more power.

00:14:20.889 --> 00:14:22.618
We can't go back to impulse,
Captain.

00:14:22.657 --> 00:14:24.090
That's how our problems started.

00:14:24.126 --> 00:14:26.094
Our best chance
is to burn the aft thrusters

00:14:26.128 --> 00:14:27.527
beyond the recommended limits.

00:14:27.562 --> 00:14:28.961
Proceed.

00:14:29.064 --> 00:14:31.498
Acknowledged. Accelerating
deuterium to rear thrusters.

00:14:31.533 --> 00:14:33.763
We have a complement
of 38 photon torpedoes

00:14:33.802 --> 00:14:35.064
at our disposal, Captain.

00:14:35.103 --> 00:14:37.162
And no way to replace them
after they're gone.

00:14:37.205 --> 00:14:39.571
Aft thrusters at 105 percent.

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:43.168
115 percent.

00:14:43.211 --> 00:14:45.475
Barrier still holding.

00:14:45.514 --> 00:14:46.708
We need something else.

00:14:46.748 --> 00:14:48.841
Give me a two-second blast
from the forward phaser bank.

00:14:48.884 --> 00:14:50.579
Firing phasers.

00:14:53.121 --> 00:14:55.487
The barrier is undamaged,
Captain.

00:14:57.092 --> 00:14:58.116
Ready a photon.

00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.286
Mr. Paris, assuming

00:14:59.327 --> 00:15:01.420
we can breach
the energy barrier,

00:15:01.463 --> 00:15:03.488
it's likely to close as
fast as the first time.

00:15:03.532 --> 00:15:05.329
I'll be riding the tail
of our torpedo, Captain.

00:15:05.367 --> 00:15:06.800
Torpedo is loaded.

00:15:06.835 --> 00:15:08.632
Align coordinates
along ship's heading.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.160
Coordinates set.

00:15:11.473 --> 00:15:12.906
Fire.

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:24.584
50,000 kilometers
to the perimeter.

00:15:24.619 --> 00:15:27.816
I'm having trouble navigating
through the energy currents.

00:15:27.856 --> 00:15:30.450
It's as thick as
a Toarian ice storm out there.

00:15:30.492 --> 00:15:32.960
35,000 kilometers to perimeter.

00:15:33.061 --> 00:15:34.961
Energy reserves
are still falling.

00:15:35.063 --> 00:15:36.997
15,000 kilometers.

00:15:42.037 --> 00:15:43.732
We've cleared the central mass.

00:15:43.772 --> 00:15:45.637
Stand down Red Alert.

00:15:45.674 --> 00:15:47.972
Take us to 2,000 kilometers
off the perimeter

00:15:48.043 --> 00:15:49.271
and hold position.

00:15:49.311 --> 00:15:51.438
Get a sample of that matter
off the hull

00:15:51.479 --> 00:15:52.969
for Lieutenant Torres
to analyze.

00:15:53.081 --> 00:15:54.139
I'd like to know what it was

00:15:54.182 --> 00:15:56.582
that humbled every
defense system on this ship.

00:15:56.618 --> 00:15:59.212
How much of our energy reserves
did we lose, Ensign?

00:15:59.254 --> 00:16:01.119
11 percent, Captain.

00:16:02.757 --> 00:16:05.419
I'm just going to have
to give up coffee.

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:07.052
That's all there is to it.

00:16:32.387 --> 00:16:33.581
Dark enough for you?

00:16:33.622 --> 00:16:34.714
What?

00:16:34.756 --> 00:16:36.155
Get up, Harry.

00:16:36.191 --> 00:16:37.419
There's something
you got to see.

00:16:37.459 --> 00:16:38.824
See?

00:16:38.860 --> 00:16:41.226
How'd you get in here?

00:16:41.263 --> 00:16:44.721
You'd be surprised
the things you learn in prison.

00:16:49.204 --> 00:16:50.432
MacAllister...

00:16:50.472 --> 00:16:51.962
James Mooney MacAllister.

00:16:52.007 --> 00:16:53.440
The guy never slept.

00:16:53.475 --> 00:16:55.841
He'd be studying
his algorithms until dawn,

00:16:55.877 --> 00:16:57.276
and the only way
I could get any sleep

00:16:57.312 --> 00:16:58.336
was to wear a mask.

00:16:58.380 --> 00:16:59.813
You could've changed roommates.

00:16:59.848 --> 00:17:00.974
Are you kidding?

00:17:01.082 --> 00:17:03.744
MacAllister got me through
fourth year quantum chemistry.

00:17:03.785 --> 00:17:05.753
Besides, I got used
to wearing it.

00:17:05.787 --> 00:17:07.448
Something about it

00:17:07.489 --> 00:17:09.320
that reminds me
of being in the womb.

00:17:09.357 --> 00:17:12.258
Harry, in order to be
reminded of something,

00:17:12.294 --> 00:17:13.283
you have to first...

00:17:13.328 --> 00:17:15.353
I remember being
in my mother's womb.

00:17:15.397 --> 00:17:16.421
Right.

00:17:16.464 --> 00:17:17.726
I do.

00:17:17.766 --> 00:17:19.666
So what is it
you have to show me?

00:17:19.701 --> 00:17:21.396
Nothing that's going to compare

00:17:21.436 --> 00:17:23.301
to that memory
of your mother's womb.

00:17:23.338 --> 00:17:28.037
Computer, activate
holodeck program Paris-3.

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:50.395
Hey, it's Tom.

00:17:50.432 --> 00:17:52.059
Welcome, Tom, welcome.

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:54.625
Hey, Tom, how you doing?

00:17:54.669 --> 00:17:56.068
What do you think, Harry?

00:17:56.104 --> 00:17:57.765
What is it, a French bistro?

00:17:57.806 --> 00:17:58.773
This is where I spent

00:17:58.807 --> 00:18:00.798
most of my second semester
at the Academy.

00:18:00.842 --> 00:18:03.242
I chose the Starfleet base
outside of Marseilles

00:18:03.278 --> 00:18:04.609
for my physical training.

00:18:04.646 --> 00:18:07.274
I always had a thing
about the French.

00:18:07.315 --> 00:18:10.011
And the French
always had a thing

00:18:10.051 --> 00:18:12.144
about you, Monsieur Thomas.

00:18:12.187 --> 00:18:14.121
And with a name like Paris,

00:18:14.155 --> 00:18:15.713
and a face like that,

00:18:15.757 --> 00:18:18.225
how could anyone resist, huh?

00:18:18.259 --> 00:18:20.591
Sandrine, this is my friend,
Harry Kim.

00:18:20.628 --> 00:18:21.925
Enchanté.

00:18:21.997 --> 00:18:23.430
Sandrine owns the place.

00:18:23.465 --> 00:18:25.296
It's been in her family
over 600 years.

00:18:25.333 --> 00:18:26.925
Tommy.

00:18:26.968 --> 00:18:28.731
It's about time.

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:30.795
I've been waiting for you.

00:18:30.839 --> 00:18:34.366
This is Ricky.

00:18:34.409 --> 00:18:37.503
I include her in all
my holo-programs.

00:18:37.545 --> 00:18:39.740
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:18:42.717 --> 00:18:43.877
Mmm...

00:18:43.918 --> 00:18:47.581
Your friend the gigolo
wouldn't leave me alone.

00:18:47.622 --> 00:18:49.749
It's what I do, Tom.

00:18:49.791 --> 00:18:51.281
Nothing personal.

00:18:51.326 --> 00:18:54.318
French father,
Daliwakan mother.

00:18:54.362 --> 00:18:57.798
She just sits there
and waits for you, huh?

00:18:57.832 --> 00:18:59.129
Like a little puppy dog.

00:18:59.167 --> 00:19:00.828
I wouldn't have it
any other way.

00:19:00.869 --> 00:19:02.336
Oh, really?

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:05.100
I thought you liked your women
with a little bite.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:08.234
Everyone knows
about your bite, Sandrine.

00:19:08.276 --> 00:19:11.245
It's when you start
sucking blood they get scared.

00:19:13.748 --> 00:19:18.242
Monsieur, can I get you
something to drink?

00:19:18.286 --> 00:19:20.777
Just a cup of tea.

00:19:21.956 --> 00:19:24.550
Harry, this is France.

00:19:24.592 --> 00:19:27.493
Uh, break open a bottle
of that '46 Saint Emilion

00:19:27.529 --> 00:19:29.394
you save behind the bar for me.

00:19:29.431 --> 00:19:32.195
I don't like to drink
this late at night.

00:19:32.233 --> 00:19:33.723
I get an acid heartburn.

00:19:33.768 --> 00:19:36.601
Harry, it's holographic wine.

00:19:36.638 --> 00:19:37.935
It doesn't give you acid.

00:19:38.006 --> 00:19:39.496
Try to get in the mood, huh?

00:19:39.541 --> 00:19:40.701
Sorry.

00:19:40.742 --> 00:19:44.200
I learned a great deal
that semester at the Academy.

00:19:44.245 --> 00:19:45.644
Most of it right here.

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:49.377
Oui... and most of it
from me.

00:19:49.417 --> 00:19:51.851
I found this place
just after my pocket was picked

00:19:51.886 --> 00:19:52.944
walking by the harbor.

00:19:52.987 --> 00:19:55.478
Somebody picked
your pocket on Earth?

00:19:55.523 --> 00:19:57.423
Oh, they just do it
for tourists.

00:19:57.459 --> 00:19:58.653
They give it back.

00:19:58.693 --> 00:20:00.126
Most of the time.

00:20:00.161 --> 00:20:01.788
Nine ball in the corner pocket.

00:20:03.965 --> 00:20:05.762
You see that pool table, Harry?

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:07.734
The table at Sandrine's
at Marseilles

00:20:07.769 --> 00:20:10.101
has attracted the world's
greatest hustlers

00:20:10.138 --> 00:20:11.571
throughout the centuries.

00:20:11.606 --> 00:20:13.073
I thought it might
be fun to program in

00:20:13.108 --> 00:20:14.632
some of the great
players to shoot with.

00:20:14.676 --> 00:20:16.667
Eight ball in the cross side.

00:20:23.718 --> 00:20:27.984
Gaunt Gary, Ames Pool Hall,
New York City, 1953.

00:20:28.056 --> 00:20:30.320
They say that he hustled

00:20:30.358 --> 00:20:31.659
the great Willie Moscone
himself.

00:20:31.792 --> 00:20:33.919
Moscone?

00:20:33.961 --> 00:20:35.792
Was he some famous
billiard player?

00:20:35.829 --> 00:20:37.660
Game is pool, kid.

00:20:37.698 --> 00:20:39.256
Pool.

00:20:39.299 --> 00:20:42.359
I don't suppose you'd care
to wager a fin on a game or two?

00:20:42.403 --> 00:20:45.463
Oh, he's not ready
for you yet, Gary.

00:20:45.506 --> 00:20:47.098
Let me teach him
a few tricks first.

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:51.478
Watch out for him, kid.

00:20:51.512 --> 00:20:54.345
He can swallow your wallet
without ever losing his smile.

00:20:55.949 --> 00:20:56.938
I'll keep it in mind.

00:20:56.984 --> 00:20:58.451
What's a fin?

00:20:58.485 --> 00:21:00.476
I'm not sure.

00:21:00.521 --> 00:21:03.456
Some old kind
of Scandinavian currency.

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:04.957
Come on.

00:21:04.992 --> 00:21:05.959
I'll rack them up.

00:21:05.993 --> 00:21:07.756
You pick out a cue.

00:21:11.632 --> 00:21:14.430
Harry, this is my idea of home.

00:21:14.468 --> 00:21:17.801
My little piece of Earth
out here in the Delta Quadrant.

00:21:20.607 --> 00:21:22.268
You shrug it off...

00:21:22.309 --> 00:21:24.209
or you like to make
the rest of us think

00:21:24.244 --> 00:21:26.235
you're shrugging it off...

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:28.373
but you miss it, too, don't you?

00:21:29.917 --> 00:21:31.942
What?

00:21:32.953 --> 00:21:34.284
Home.

00:21:37.458 --> 00:21:38.891
Your shot, Harry.

00:22:09.823 --> 00:22:12.690
Computer, activate emergency
medical holographic program.

00:22:12.726 --> 00:22:15.217
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:22:15.262 --> 00:22:17.958
Why do you always
have to say that?

00:22:18.031 --> 00:22:20.591
I can only speculate about
my programmer's motives.

00:22:20.634 --> 00:22:22.568
Perhaps he thought
I might be summoned

00:22:22.603 --> 00:22:23.934
for... important reasons.

00:22:23.971 --> 00:22:25.529
Under the circumstances,
don't you think

00:22:25.572 --> 00:22:27.130
you really ought
to change your program?

00:22:27.174 --> 00:22:28.732
Now, there's
an interesting concept...

00:22:28.776 --> 00:22:31.210
a hologram
that programs himself.

00:22:31.245 --> 00:22:33.543
What would I do
with that ability?

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:35.411
Create a family,
raise an army...

00:22:35.449 --> 00:22:37.246
I know a little about
holographic programming.

00:22:37.284 --> 00:22:39.684
I could probably
reprogram you.

00:22:39.720 --> 00:22:41.984
That makes me feel
particularly confident.

00:22:42.055 --> 00:22:44.148
Has anyone ever told you,
you have a lousy attitude?

00:22:44.191 --> 00:22:45.556
If you don't like
the doctor's attitude,

00:22:45.592 --> 00:22:46.854
there's a man sitting
at a console

00:22:46.894 --> 00:22:48.623
in the Jupiter Station
Holo-programming Center

00:22:48.662 --> 00:22:49.720
you can write to.

00:22:49.763 --> 00:22:50.957
His name is Zimmerman.

00:22:50.998 --> 00:22:53.193
He looks a lot like me,
actually.

00:22:53.233 --> 00:22:55.963
Now, not that I don't
enjoy the repartee,

00:22:56.003 --> 00:22:58.437
but was there a reason
you stopped in?

00:22:58.472 --> 00:23:00.372
I need a second opinion on this.

00:23:00.407 --> 00:23:01.772
Who gave you the first opinion?

00:23:01.809 --> 00:23:03.174
I gave it to myself.

00:23:03.210 --> 00:23:05.872
It's a sample of residue
we picked up in a nebula.

00:23:05.913 --> 00:23:06.880
A nebula?

00:23:06.914 --> 00:23:08.541
What were we doing in a nebula?

00:23:08.582 --> 00:23:09.947
No, wait, don't tell me.

00:23:10.017 --> 00:23:12.349
We were investigating.

00:23:12.386 --> 00:23:14.183
That's all we do around here.

00:23:14.221 --> 00:23:15.848
Why pretend
we're going home at all?

00:23:15.889 --> 00:23:17.322
All we're going to do
is investigate

00:23:17.357 --> 00:23:19.450
every cubic millimeter
of this Quadrant, aren't we?

00:23:19.493 --> 00:23:21.654
The molecules are isolinear.

00:23:21.695 --> 00:23:23.595
No polycyclic structures, but...

00:23:23.630 --> 00:23:27.828
But this is what brought
you to me, isn't it?

00:23:27.868 --> 00:23:29.836
The nucleogenic peptide bonds.

00:23:29.870 --> 00:23:32.964
Is it some kind
of phospholipid fiber?

00:23:34.474 --> 00:23:36.601
And you were doing so well.

00:23:37.611 --> 00:23:39.545
Now... I suspect it's something

00:23:39.580 --> 00:23:41.946
far more interesting than that.

00:23:46.553 --> 00:23:47.713
Come in.

00:23:47.754 --> 00:23:50.723
Repair crews have degaussed
the hull, Captain.

00:23:50.757 --> 00:23:53.419
Good. Let's plan
an 0700 departure.

00:23:53.460 --> 00:23:55.223
What's this?

00:23:55.262 --> 00:23:57.992
My medicine bundle.

00:23:58.031 --> 00:24:01.159
I've never shown it
to anyone before.

00:24:01.201 --> 00:24:02.498
After what you said
this morning,

00:24:02.536 --> 00:24:04.834
I thought it was important
to let you see.

00:24:04.872 --> 00:24:07.568
Will it help me find
my animal guide?

00:24:07.608 --> 00:24:09.132
Eventually,
you'll have to assemble

00:24:09.176 --> 00:24:10.336
your own medicine bundle,

00:24:10.377 --> 00:24:12.072
but this will allow me
to assist you

00:24:12.112 --> 00:24:13.443
in your quest for a guide.

00:24:14.815 --> 00:24:15.873
Now?

00:24:19.853 --> 00:24:20.911
Now.

00:24:48.081 --> 00:24:51.209
A blackbird's wing...

00:24:51.251 --> 00:24:53.947
a stone from the river...

00:24:53.987 --> 00:24:56.182
an akoonah.

00:24:56.223 --> 00:24:57.815
"Akoonah"?

00:24:57.858 --> 00:25:00.258
My ancestors used
psychoactive herbs

00:25:00.294 --> 00:25:01.852
to assist their vision quests.

00:25:01.895 --> 00:25:04.625
Now they're no longer necessary.

00:25:04.665 --> 00:25:06.792
Our scientists have found
more modern ways

00:25:06.833 --> 00:25:08.801
to facilitate the search
for animal guides.

00:25:09.870 --> 00:25:11.929
Place your hand on it.

00:25:12.005 --> 00:25:14.940
And concentrate on the stone.

00:25:18.245 --> 00:25:19.803
A- koo-chee-moya.

00:25:19.846 --> 00:25:23.839
We are far from the sacred
places of our grandfathers.

00:25:23.884 --> 00:25:27.149
We are far
from the bones of our people,

00:25:27.187 --> 00:25:29.849
but perhaps there is
one powerful being

00:25:29.890 --> 00:25:31.915
who will embrace this woman

00:25:31.959 --> 00:25:34.689
and give her
the answers she seeks.

00:25:34.728 --> 00:25:36.787
Allow your eyes to close.

00:25:38.765 --> 00:25:41.700
Breathe to feel
the light in your belly

00:25:41.735 --> 00:25:46.638
and let it expand
until the light is everywhere.

00:25:48.141 --> 00:25:51.201
Prepare yourself
to leave this room

00:25:51.244 --> 00:25:53.303
and this ship,

00:25:53.347 --> 00:25:55.542
and return to a place

00:25:55.582 --> 00:25:59.848
where you were the most content
and peaceful you have ever been.

00:26:01.421 --> 00:26:03.821
You can see all around you

00:26:03.857 --> 00:26:05.882
and hear the sounds
of this place.

00:26:12.399 --> 00:26:14.390
I know this place.

00:26:14.434 --> 00:26:16.265
It's...

00:26:16.303 --> 00:26:18.203
You must not discuss with me
what you see,

00:26:18.238 --> 00:26:20.570
or you will offend
your animal guide.

00:26:22.576 --> 00:26:25.340
As you continue to look around,

00:26:25.379 --> 00:26:26.869
you will become aware
of other life

00:26:26.913 --> 00:26:29.108
that shares
this place with you.

00:26:29.149 --> 00:26:32.209
It will be the first animal
you see.

00:26:32.252 --> 00:26:33.947
That is the one
you will speak to.

00:26:34.054 --> 00:26:36.181
Do you see an animal?

00:26:44.229 --> 00:26:45.560
Yes.

00:26:45.597 --> 00:26:48.191
Speak to it.

00:26:48.233 --> 00:26:50.963
What do I say?

00:26:51.003 --> 00:26:53.494
You know what you want to ask.

00:26:58.076 --> 00:26:59.543
I'm sorry.

00:26:59.578 --> 00:27:01.876
I should've asked the computer
for no interruptions.

00:27:01.914 --> 00:27:03.609
Come in.

00:27:05.651 --> 00:27:09.052
The Commander was introducing
me to my animal guide.

00:27:09.087 --> 00:27:10.384
I hope

00:27:10.422 --> 00:27:12.049
that you have
better luck with yours

00:27:12.090 --> 00:27:13.057
than I had with mine.

00:27:13.091 --> 00:27:14.752
B'Elanna's the only one I know

00:27:14.793 --> 00:27:16.852
who tried to kill
her animal guide.

00:27:16.895 --> 00:27:17.862
I'm sorry

00:27:17.896 --> 00:27:19.227
to interrupt,
but the Doctor and I

00:27:19.264 --> 00:27:21.095
have come up with a rather
surprising analysis

00:27:21.133 --> 00:27:22.395
of the matter
left on the hull.

00:27:24.403 --> 00:27:25.927
It's organic.

00:27:26.004 --> 00:27:28.063
Microscopic life-forms
from the nebula.

00:27:28.106 --> 00:27:29.073
That's not what I mean.

00:27:29.107 --> 00:27:30.131
The samples are clearly

00:27:30.175 --> 00:27:33.076
organic elements
of a much larger life-form.

00:27:33.111 --> 00:27:35.102
It appears, Captain,
that this nebula

00:27:35.147 --> 00:27:36.444
is not a nebula at all.

00:27:46.358 --> 00:27:47.620
I'm curious, Captain.

00:27:47.659 --> 00:27:49.126
Exactly what are you
looking for?

00:27:49.161 --> 00:27:50.128
I need to know

00:27:50.162 --> 00:27:52.460
if we did serious harm
to this life-form.

00:27:52.497 --> 00:27:55.489
Let's see... you ran
your ship through it,

00:27:55.534 --> 00:27:56.728
fired phasers at it,

00:27:56.768 --> 00:27:58.531
and blew a hole in it
with a photon torpedo.

00:27:58.570 --> 00:28:00.401
I'd say it's a pretty good
chance that you...

00:28:00.439 --> 00:28:02.634
Computer, mute audio.

00:28:02.674 --> 00:28:04.869
Isolate that concentration
of omicron particles

00:28:04.910 --> 00:28:06.104
we were trying to get to.

00:28:06.144 --> 00:28:07.338
That would be right here.

00:28:07.379 --> 00:28:09.074
Mr. Tuvok?

00:28:09.114 --> 00:28:11.139
I'm afraid the concentration
of particles

00:28:11.183 --> 00:28:12.616
is far lower
than I originally observed.

00:28:12.651 --> 00:28:15.119
Furthermore, it appears
that many of the particles

00:28:15.153 --> 00:28:17.246
have now moved outside
the energy barrier.

00:28:17.289 --> 00:28:20.224
Is it possible they're leaking
out through the breach we made?

00:28:20.258 --> 00:28:22.283
That would be
a logical conclusion.

00:28:22.327 --> 00:28:23.726
It's also a logical conclusion

00:28:23.762 --> 00:28:25.753
that all of the phenomena
we've encountered

00:28:25.797 --> 00:28:29.130
were actually this life-form's
natural defense systems.

00:28:29.167 --> 00:28:31.897
The way the barrier was
protecting the omicron particles

00:28:31.937 --> 00:28:34.235
almost suggests we were
entering a vital organ.

00:28:34.272 --> 00:28:35.933
So, it seems very clear

00:28:36.008 --> 00:28:38.033
that we've severely hurt
an innocent life-form.

00:28:38.076 --> 00:28:40.237
How do we repair
the harm we've done?

00:28:40.278 --> 00:28:41.870
Uh, Captain?

00:28:43.215 --> 00:28:45.649
Computer, resume audio.

00:28:45.684 --> 00:28:46.912
How kind of you.

00:28:46.952 --> 00:28:49.420
You may be interested to know
that the analysis

00:28:49.454 --> 00:28:50.682
of the organic sample

00:28:50.722 --> 00:28:53.953
suggested this life-form
has the capacity to regenerate.

00:28:54.059 --> 00:28:56.892
The process may simply
need a helping hand.

00:28:56.928 --> 00:29:00.056
Any ideas how we could
stimulate regeneration?

00:29:00.098 --> 00:29:01.895
Lieutenant Torres
has the answer.

00:29:03.135 --> 00:29:04.466
I do?

00:29:04.503 --> 00:29:07.165
You were the one who first
observed that this life-form has

00:29:07.205 --> 00:29:08.900
a nucleogenic structure.

00:29:08.940 --> 00:29:13.639
If the life-form has
a nucleogenic structure...

00:29:15.247 --> 00:29:16.646
nucleonic radiation

00:29:16.682 --> 00:29:18.547
ought to assist
its healing process.

00:29:18.583 --> 00:29:22.679
A nucleonic beam along
the edges of the breach

00:29:22.721 --> 00:29:25.383
should theoretically
promote regeneration.

00:29:25.424 --> 00:29:27.858
Bravo.

00:29:27.893 --> 00:29:30.453
Commander, take us
to Yellow Alert

00:29:30.495 --> 00:29:31.462
and advise the crew

00:29:31.496 --> 00:29:33.930
that we're going to reenter
the life-form.

00:29:33.965 --> 00:29:37.492
Mr. Kim, review all systems
in light of our first experience

00:29:37.536 --> 00:29:40.437
and see if you can
provide new safeguards.

00:29:40.472 --> 00:29:44.033
Tuvok, your job is to find
some modification of the shields

00:29:44.076 --> 00:29:47.603
that will hold off this life-
form's natural defense systems.

00:29:47.646 --> 00:29:50.171
We begin at 1300 hours.

00:29:50.215 --> 00:29:52.080
Dismissed.

00:29:52.117 --> 00:29:55.951
The bantan is a little
on the spicy side.

00:29:55.987 --> 00:29:58.956
Kes grows them herself
in the hydroponic garden.

00:29:59.057 --> 00:30:01.218
Don't eat any
of the little pink things

00:30:01.259 --> 00:30:02.385
and you'll be fine.

00:30:02.427 --> 00:30:04.224
All personnel
report to stations.

00:30:04.262 --> 00:30:05.456
Yellow Alert.

00:30:05.497 --> 00:30:08.432
Now what?
Neelix to Chakotay.

00:30:08.467 --> 00:30:09.957
We're very busy up here, Neelix.

00:30:10.001 --> 00:30:10.968
What do you need?

00:30:11.002 --> 00:30:12.401
This Yellow Alert business...

00:30:12.437 --> 00:30:14.234
I was just starting...

00:30:14.272 --> 00:30:16.536
Sorry. We found out that the
nebula is actually a life-form

00:30:16.575 --> 00:30:18.975
and we've got to go back in to
repair some damage we did to it.

00:30:19.077 --> 00:30:19.975
Chakotay out.

00:30:20.078 --> 00:30:21.841
Go back in? Hello?

00:30:21.880 --> 00:30:23.780
Well, that's it!
I've had it!

00:30:23.815 --> 00:30:24.782
Neelix...

00:30:24.816 --> 00:30:27.046
No! I'm going
to the Captain about this.

00:30:29.054 --> 00:30:30.715
Come in.

00:30:32.324 --> 00:30:33.450
Captain, I understand

00:30:33.492 --> 00:30:35.255
that this nebula
we've discovered

00:30:35.293 --> 00:30:36.954
is some kind of monster?

00:30:36.995 --> 00:30:39.759
Not a monster, Neelix,
but it is a life-form.

00:30:39.798 --> 00:30:41.163
Excuse me if I sound crazy,

00:30:41.199 --> 00:30:43.759
because someone may have been
playing a joke on me,

00:30:43.802 --> 00:30:45.133
but you aren't planning

00:30:45.170 --> 00:30:48.333
to take us back into the belly
of this beast, are you?

00:30:48.373 --> 00:30:49.772
No joke.

00:30:49.808 --> 00:30:50.797
Why?

00:30:50.842 --> 00:30:52.366
Because we hurt it

00:30:52.410 --> 00:30:54.844
and we have to help it recover.

00:30:54.880 --> 00:30:56.609
I did not come on board

00:30:56.648 --> 00:30:58.343
this ship to be
a veterinarian, Captain.

00:30:58.383 --> 00:31:00.681
And I thought you were
a man of unlimited talents.

00:31:00.719 --> 00:31:03.711
I just reached my limit.

00:31:03.755 --> 00:31:04.722
So, if you don't mind,

00:31:04.756 --> 00:31:06.815
Kes and I will wait on board
my little vessel

00:31:06.858 --> 00:31:08.450
for you to return.

00:31:08.493 --> 00:31:11.087
All our crews are busy
preparing for this mission.

00:31:11.129 --> 00:31:12.858
I'm not pulling them
off their duties

00:31:12.898 --> 00:31:14.388
to prepare your ship for launch,

00:31:14.432 --> 00:31:16.730
and I'm not going to drop you
off on the side of the road

00:31:16.768 --> 00:31:17.928
every time we hit a bump.

00:31:17.969 --> 00:31:20.096
When we're finished,
if you want to leave,

00:31:20.138 --> 00:31:21.901
that's your business,
but for the moment,

00:31:21.940 --> 00:31:23.532
find yourself
a seat with a good view

00:31:23.575 --> 00:31:27.602
because, just like Jonah
and the whale, you're going in.

00:31:29.080 --> 00:31:30.877
Is that final?

00:31:30.915 --> 00:31:32.610
Dismissed.

00:31:35.853 --> 00:31:39.880
That's a Starfleet expression
for "get out."

00:31:45.029 --> 00:31:47.122
Jonah?

00:31:47.165 --> 00:31:48.826
Whale?

00:31:57.508 --> 00:32:00.136
Approaching the perimeter.

00:32:00.178 --> 00:32:01.873
Disengage impulse engines.

00:32:03.214 --> 00:32:05.774
Impulse engines off-line.

00:32:05.817 --> 00:32:08.149
Engage thrusters, one-third.

00:32:08.186 --> 00:32:09.619
Thrusters engaged.

00:32:09.654 --> 00:32:11.417
Red Alert.

00:32:14.659 --> 00:32:15.887
Shields are up.

00:32:15.927 --> 00:32:17.827
Adaptive harmonics
are operational.

00:32:17.862 --> 00:32:19.295
Density is already
more than double

00:32:19.330 --> 00:32:20.592
what we encountered last time.

00:32:20.631 --> 00:32:22.826
EM hull pressure is approaching
dangerous levels, Captain.

00:32:22.867 --> 00:32:23.834
Mr. Kim?

00:32:23.868 --> 00:32:24.926
If my research is right,

00:32:24.969 --> 00:32:26.960
releasing positive ions
through the nacelles

00:32:27.005 --> 00:32:28.836
should repel
some of the dust out there.

00:32:28.873 --> 00:32:31.068
Without causing further harm
to the creature?

00:32:31.109 --> 00:32:32.406
I believe so, Captain.

00:32:32.443 --> 00:32:33.967
Very well.

00:32:36.147 --> 00:32:37.944
Ion release confirmed.

00:32:39.450 --> 00:32:41.975
Ambient density is dropping.

00:32:42.053 --> 00:32:45.113
Hull pressure
is decreasing also.

00:32:45.156 --> 00:32:47.021
Hold your course.

00:32:48.526 --> 00:32:50.858
14,000 kilometers to the breach.

00:32:51.996 --> 00:32:53.964
I can see it.

00:32:53.998 --> 00:32:55.158
Magnify.

00:32:59.470 --> 00:33:01.734
Engineering,
ready your nucleonic beam.

00:33:01.773 --> 00:33:03.798
Ready and awaiting your orders,
Captain.

00:33:03.841 --> 00:33:06.435
Mr. Paris,
bring us into position.

00:33:06.477 --> 00:33:08.775
Coming about 40 degrees.

00:33:11.816 --> 00:33:13.215
Report!

00:33:14.318 --> 00:33:17.344
We're being hit by some
kind of multi-polar charges.

00:33:18.556 --> 00:33:20.353
They're not like anything
we saw the first time.

00:33:20.391 --> 00:33:21.881
Shields at 87 percent.

00:33:21.926 --> 00:33:22.950
Will they hold?

00:33:23.027 --> 00:33:24.824
The polarity of each charge
is rotating so quickly,

00:33:24.862 --> 00:33:25.954
the shields cannot compensate.

00:33:25.997 --> 00:33:28.966
We've lost
the rear driver coil assembly.

00:33:29.000 --> 00:33:30.695
Inertial dampers are off-line.

00:33:30.735 --> 00:33:31.929
I'm losing control.

00:33:31.969 --> 00:33:33.937
Hold on!

00:33:42.980 --> 00:33:46.381
Engineering, initiate emergency
shutdown of all thrusters.

00:33:46.417 --> 00:33:49.545
Captain, the only way
we can shut down all thrusters

00:33:49.587 --> 00:33:51.316
is to vent the deuterium
into space.

00:33:51.355 --> 00:33:53.585
We can't afford
to lose all that fuel.

00:33:53.624 --> 00:33:55.148
We have no choice.
Do it!

00:33:55.193 --> 00:33:57.991
Acknowledged.
Cutting thrusters.

00:33:58.062 --> 00:34:00.656
Inertial dampers
are still off-line.

00:34:00.698 --> 00:34:05.226
Reset IDF baseline at 3-0-0
and reinitialize.

00:34:05.269 --> 00:34:07.260
Field processors
coming back on line.

00:34:07.305 --> 00:34:10.399
Inertial damping restored.

00:34:10.441 --> 00:34:12.375
All stop.
Damage report.

00:34:12.410 --> 00:34:15.106
Electro-plasma leaks
reported on Deck 14.

00:34:15.146 --> 00:34:16.773
Repair crews are
being dispatched.

00:34:16.814 --> 00:34:19.044
Otherwise, we seem
to be in one piece.

00:34:19.083 --> 00:34:21.779
I believe the optical data
network is down, Ensign.

00:34:22.987 --> 00:34:25.319
Yes, sir.
I'll get right on it.

00:34:26.924 --> 00:34:29.859
14 injuries reported, Captain...
none serious.

00:34:29.894 --> 00:34:32.192
Have any idea where we are,
Mr. Paris?

00:34:32.230 --> 00:34:35.927
Approximately 70,000 kilometers
from our former position...

00:34:35.967 --> 00:34:38.561
deeper inside the creature
than before.

00:34:39.971 --> 00:34:42.462
Let's hope it has
a slow digestive process.

00:34:42.507 --> 00:34:44.168
Yes, ma'am.

00:34:44.208 --> 00:34:45.334
We need to get back

00:34:45.376 --> 00:34:47.344
to the wound
without causing a response

00:34:47.378 --> 00:34:49.846
from its defense systems.
Suggestions?

00:34:49.881 --> 00:34:51.473
It seems to be leaving us alone

00:34:51.516 --> 00:34:53.916
now that we've cut off
all propulsion systems.

00:34:53.951 --> 00:34:55.976
Maybe that's what cues it
to respond.

00:34:56.087 --> 00:34:58.180
If I'm right, we might
be able to get back

00:34:58.222 --> 00:34:59.712
without engaging any engines.

00:34:59.757 --> 00:35:00.746
No engines?

00:35:00.791 --> 00:35:01.883
We've been reading

00:35:01.926 --> 00:35:04.554
these swirling energy currents
since we first got here.

00:35:04.595 --> 00:35:05.857
When we thought it was a nebula,

00:35:05.897 --> 00:35:07.489
we weren't looking
for any pattern.

00:35:07.532 --> 00:35:08.931
We thought they were
just random eddies.

00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:11.662
But now, I'm wondering
if these currents

00:35:11.702 --> 00:35:14.432
might be some kind
of a circulatory system.

00:35:14.472 --> 00:35:17.964
Mr. Kim, are you showing omicron
particles in these currents?

00:35:21.712 --> 00:35:23.009
Affirmative, Captain.

00:35:24.549 --> 00:35:26.779
If the currents are distributing
omicron energy

00:35:26.817 --> 00:35:27.943
throughout the life-form,

00:35:28.052 --> 00:35:31.419
the circulatory system
might pass right by that wound.

00:35:31.455 --> 00:35:33.582
We could get in one
of those currents

00:35:33.624 --> 00:35:35.251
and surf back.

00:35:35.293 --> 00:35:37.352
Use the reaction
control thrusters

00:35:37.395 --> 00:35:39.727
in drift mode only, Mr. Paris.

00:35:39.764 --> 00:35:41.254
Aye, Captain.

00:35:41.299 --> 00:35:43.859
We're on our way.

00:35:43.901 --> 00:35:48.861
Speed... all of 200 kph.

00:35:48.906 --> 00:35:50.669
Time for refreshment.

00:35:50.708 --> 00:35:55.270
Ailis pâté,
Felada onion crisps,

00:35:55.313 --> 00:35:57.679
stuffed Cardaway leaves.

00:35:57.715 --> 00:35:59.706
I appreciate the thought,
Neelix,

00:35:59.750 --> 00:36:01.308
but this is hardly the time.

00:36:01.352 --> 00:36:03.445
As the morale officer
on this ship,

00:36:03.487 --> 00:36:04.920
I insist that a break
in the workload

00:36:04.956 --> 00:36:06.514
is both healthy
and necessary.

00:36:06.557 --> 00:36:08.616
Go on, Mr. Vulcan.

00:36:08.659 --> 00:36:10.650
It might even
help you loosen up.

00:36:12.263 --> 00:36:13.924
Or not.

00:36:13.998 --> 00:36:16.796
May I ask when you
became morale officer?

00:36:16.834 --> 00:36:18.597
Oh, just a few minutes ago,

00:36:18.636 --> 00:36:21.230
when I sensed crew morale
might be especially low.

00:36:21.272 --> 00:36:22.603
Mine certainly was.

00:36:22.640 --> 00:36:24.267
We were in a free fall
at the time.

00:36:24.308 --> 00:36:26.572
Cooking always helps
Neelix to unwind.

00:36:26.611 --> 00:36:30.445
Yes, and after we stabilized
I certainly needed to unwind.

00:36:30.481 --> 00:36:31.641
So it seemed to me,

00:36:31.682 --> 00:36:33.809
I had a choice to either
come up here and say,

00:36:33.851 --> 00:36:34.840
"I told you so"...

00:36:34.885 --> 00:36:36.546
No.

00:36:36.587 --> 00:36:38.782
Or to try to do
something constructive

00:36:38.823 --> 00:36:42.224
to help out
in my own humble manner.

00:36:42.260 --> 00:36:44.194
Try the stuffed
Cardaway leaves.

00:36:44.228 --> 00:36:45.559
They're irresistible.

00:36:49.533 --> 00:36:53.526
Now, as your new morale officer,
I thought it might be fun

00:36:53.571 --> 00:36:55.334
for us all to sing
a few songs together.

00:36:55.373 --> 00:36:56.465
Don't push it, Neelix.

00:36:56.507 --> 00:36:57.804
Captain?

00:36:57.842 --> 00:36:59.475
Well done, Mr. Paris.

00:36:59.475 --> 00:37:00.703
Well done, Mr. Paris.

00:37:00.742 --> 00:37:02.505
Take us gently out
of the current.

00:37:02.544 --> 00:37:03.875
Stay in RCS drift mode.

00:37:03.912 --> 00:37:05.436
Aye, Captain.

00:37:05.481 --> 00:37:08.279
Ms. Torres,
prepare your nucleonic beam.

00:37:08.317 --> 00:37:09.909
We're ready down here, Captain.

00:37:09.985 --> 00:37:13.113
Let's give the wound
two doses to start.

00:37:13.155 --> 00:37:15.248
Five bursts
at a two-second interval.

00:37:15.290 --> 00:37:16.416
Now.

00:37:19.962 --> 00:37:21.190
Analysis.

00:37:21.230 --> 00:37:22.197
Scanners are showing

00:37:22.231 --> 00:37:25.928
the regeneration rate up
only.04 percent.

00:37:25.968 --> 00:37:27.902
I don't know
what we can hope to accomplish

00:37:27.936 --> 00:37:29.335
if this is the best we can do.

00:37:29.371 --> 00:37:31.839
The breach may simply be
too large to seal.

00:37:31.874 --> 00:37:33.637
This is the Doctor speaking.

00:37:33.675 --> 00:37:35.142
Please activate your monitor

00:37:35.177 --> 00:37:37.111
to the emergency medical
holographic channel.

00:37:37.145 --> 00:37:39.306
I believe I may have
a suggestion that will help.

00:37:42.751 --> 00:37:45.481
Since no one had the courtesy
to turn me off

00:37:45.521 --> 00:37:47.853
after my last consultation,
I've had the opportunity

00:37:47.890 --> 00:37:51.121
to observe your progress...
or lack of same.

00:37:51.159 --> 00:37:52.490
I believe a slight alteration

00:37:52.528 --> 00:37:54.155
of your treatment plan
is necessary.

00:37:54.196 --> 00:37:55.390
As inspiration, I've drawn

00:37:55.430 --> 00:37:58.228
on an ancient medical technique
known as a suture.

00:37:58.267 --> 00:37:59.666
"Suture"?

00:37:59.701 --> 00:38:01.498
Before the advent
of laser technology,

00:38:01.537 --> 00:38:04.506
surgical fiber was used
to stitch together a wound

00:38:04.540 --> 00:38:06.007
to allow it to heal naturally.

00:38:06.041 --> 00:38:07.269
How does that help us?

00:38:07.309 --> 00:38:09.903
Your ship's energy systems
are compatible

00:38:09.945 --> 00:38:12.914
with this life-form's omicron
particles, are they not?

00:38:12.981 --> 00:38:14.243
That's right.

00:38:14.283 --> 00:38:16.444
Then it is very likely
that this vessel could serve

00:38:16.485 --> 00:38:18.851
the life-form's needs in much
the same manner as a suture.

00:38:18.887 --> 00:38:19.876
By allowing the ship

00:38:19.922 --> 00:38:22.083
to serve as an energy conduit
across the wound

00:38:22.124 --> 00:38:23.386
the life-form should be able

00:38:23.425 --> 00:38:24.915
to regenerate itself
more rapidly.

00:38:25.027 --> 00:38:27.222
And how are we supposed
to get the ship into the wound

00:38:27.262 --> 00:38:29.162
without getting the hell
beat out of us again?

00:38:29.197 --> 00:38:30.824
That's your problem, not mine.

00:38:30.866 --> 00:38:32.197
Doctor out.

00:38:34.903 --> 00:38:36.666
That's sort of like
asking a hurt dog

00:38:36.705 --> 00:38:38.866
not to bite you
while you tend to its wounds.

00:38:38.907 --> 00:38:40.841
You like dogs, Mr. Paris?

00:38:42.578 --> 00:38:44.409
Yes, ma'am.
I always had a dog.

00:38:44.446 --> 00:38:46.311
I like dogs, too.

00:38:46.348 --> 00:38:49.442
When I had to clean out a cut
on my dog's leg,

00:38:49.484 --> 00:38:52.942
I needed to create
a little diversion first

00:38:53.055 --> 00:38:54.784
to take her mind off it.

00:38:54.823 --> 00:38:57.053
Mr. Kim...

00:38:57.092 --> 00:38:58.616
prepare a class-4 microprobe.

00:38:58.660 --> 00:38:59.752
Aye, Captain.

00:38:59.795 --> 00:39:00.853
Lieutenant,

00:39:00.896 --> 00:39:03.626
if I gave you a short burst
from our thrusters,

00:39:03.665 --> 00:39:05.223
would it be enough
for you to maneuver

00:39:05.267 --> 00:39:06.632
into the breach in ten seconds?

00:39:06.668 --> 00:39:08.795
I'd feel better if I had 20.

00:39:08.837 --> 00:39:10.532
Once we launch that probe
as a diversion,

00:39:10.572 --> 00:39:13.405
you might have ten,
maybe even less than that.

00:39:13.442 --> 00:39:15.910
Ten sounds good.

00:39:15.944 --> 00:39:17.639
Mr. Kim, status?

00:39:17.679 --> 00:39:19.544
Microprobe is loaded and ready.

00:39:19.581 --> 00:39:22.675
Set coordinates for launch
at 160 mark 70.

00:39:22.718 --> 00:39:24.879
Cut power after 500 meters.

00:39:24.920 --> 00:39:27.081
I don't want to hurt
this life-form again.

00:39:27.122 --> 00:39:28.214
Acknowledged.

00:39:28.256 --> 00:39:31.089
Engineering, I'll need
a one-second burst

00:39:31.126 --> 00:39:32.525
from our aft thrusters
on my order.

00:39:32.561 --> 00:39:34.028
Standing by.

00:39:34.096 --> 00:39:36.326
Launch microprobe.

00:39:40.369 --> 00:39:41.859
Thrusters.

00:39:41.903 --> 00:39:43.131
Firing!

00:39:50.178 --> 00:39:52.669
Reading mono-polar charges,
high frequency.

00:39:52.714 --> 00:39:55.114
Shields at 75 percent
and holding.

00:39:55.150 --> 00:39:56.447
Maintain position.

00:39:56.485 --> 00:39:58.578
Engineering, direct
two nucleonic beams

00:39:58.620 --> 00:40:00.417
fore and aft... parallel

00:40:00.455 --> 00:40:01.581
to the central axis of the ship.

00:40:01.623 --> 00:40:03.454
Acknowledged.
Beam engaged.

00:40:09.498 --> 00:40:13.491
Captain, I'm showing a rapid
growth pattern along the wound.

00:40:13.535 --> 00:40:15.935
Regenerative matter approaching
from both directions

00:40:15.971 --> 00:40:17.734
at just under 500 kilometers
per hour.

00:40:17.773 --> 00:40:19.365
Hold position.

00:40:19.408 --> 00:40:21.069
Captain, the shields are only
designed to withstand...

00:40:21.109 --> 00:40:22.974
I'm aware of that, Mr. Tuvok.
Hold position!

00:40:23.078 --> 00:40:24.375
Regenerative matter approaching.

00:40:24.413 --> 00:40:25.380
Range...

00:40:25.414 --> 00:40:27.245
30 kilometers... fore and aft.

00:40:27.282 --> 00:40:29.409
Engineering,
ready full thrusters.

00:40:29.451 --> 00:40:30.475
Mr. Paris?

00:40:30.519 --> 00:40:31.486
Just tell me when.

00:40:31.520 --> 00:40:34.182
Regenerative matter
at 20 kilometers.

00:40:34.222 --> 00:40:36.713
Fifteen... ten...

00:40:36.758 --> 00:40:38.817
Disengage nucleonic beam.

00:40:38.860 --> 00:40:39.952
Fire thrusters.

00:40:39.995 --> 00:40:41.553
Thrusters engaged.

00:40:41.596 --> 00:40:42.927
Now, Mr. Paris.

00:40:51.206 --> 00:40:54.107
40,000 kilometers
to the perimeter.

00:40:54.142 --> 00:40:55.769
30,000.

00:40:55.811 --> 00:40:58.302
The life-form's regeneration
rate is up 40 percent, Captain.

00:40:58.346 --> 00:41:00.644
Looks like it's well on the way
to closing that wound.

00:41:04.986 --> 00:41:06.851
We've cleared the central mass.

00:41:12.894 --> 00:41:15.124
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:41:15.163 --> 00:41:17.723
We set out
to augment our energy reserves

00:41:17.766 --> 00:41:20.667
and wound up depleting them
by over 20 percent.

00:41:20.702 --> 00:41:22.829
As a result,
we've set a new course

00:41:22.871 --> 00:41:25.362
for a planet
14 light-years away

00:41:25.407 --> 00:41:26.874
that Neelix says might have

00:41:26.908 --> 00:41:28.637
compatible energy sources
to offer us.

00:41:28.677 --> 00:41:30.736
It is out of our way,

00:41:30.779 --> 00:41:33.339
but circumstances offer
few alternatives.

00:41:33.381 --> 00:41:35.508
So much for raising spirits.

00:41:37.819 --> 00:41:39.411
Turning in for the night,
Captain?

00:41:39.454 --> 00:41:41.513
Actually, I'm going
to talk to an animal

00:41:41.556 --> 00:41:42.818
and then turn in.

00:41:42.858 --> 00:41:45.656
Something Commander
Chakotay taught me.

00:41:45.694 --> 00:41:47.355
Supposed to be
quite therapeutic.

00:41:47.395 --> 00:41:49.454
You might want
to ask him about it.

00:41:49.498 --> 00:41:50.760
I will.

00:41:54.069 --> 00:41:55.229
Captain...

00:41:55.270 --> 00:41:56.669
What is it, Ensign?

00:41:56.705 --> 00:41:59.367
Well, I don't mean
to be out of place,

00:41:59.407 --> 00:42:01.637
but if you'd care to join us,
you'd be welcome.

00:42:01.676 --> 00:42:03.906
Join you where?

00:42:09.351 --> 00:42:11.819
Come on, Tommy.
Let's get out of here.

00:42:11.853 --> 00:42:13.445
Easy, honey.

00:42:13.488 --> 00:42:15.479
I'm setting the Indian up
for the big hustle.

00:42:15.524 --> 00:42:16.684
But he's beating you.

00:42:16.725 --> 00:42:21.995
Yeah, that's exactly what
he's supposed to think, too.

00:42:23.863 --> 00:42:25.626
As you were.

00:42:25.665 --> 00:42:30.329
Well... this is remarkable.

00:42:30.370 --> 00:42:34.739
Mr. Kim tells me this is
your doing, Mr. Paris.

00:42:34.774 --> 00:42:35.832
Ah... yeah.

00:42:35.875 --> 00:42:39.333
It's just a little
diversion, Captain.

00:42:39.379 --> 00:42:40.539
One always knows

00:42:40.580 --> 00:42:43.845
when a woman of good
breeding enters a room.

00:42:43.883 --> 00:42:46.351
Ma chérie...

00:42:46.386 --> 00:42:49.184
may I request
your favorite song,

00:42:49.222 --> 00:42:52.123
so that we may dance,
before I take you

00:42:52.158 --> 00:42:54.251
to my private felucca
on the wharf

00:42:54.293 --> 00:42:57.262
and make passionate
love to you?

00:42:57.296 --> 00:42:59.127
Uh... I'm sorry.

00:42:59.165 --> 00:43:01.929
If I had some kind of warning
that you were coming...

00:43:01.968 --> 00:43:02.935
You would have changed it,

00:43:02.969 --> 00:43:04.493
and I would have missed
all the fun.

00:43:07.407 --> 00:43:09.398
I just don't know
what the dolls see

00:43:09.442 --> 00:43:10.602
in a gigolo, do you?

00:43:10.643 --> 00:43:13.305
Now, me, I got a whole
different approach to women.

00:43:13.346 --> 00:43:16.406
Treat a lady like a tramp,
and a tramp like a lady.

00:43:16.449 --> 00:43:17.575
Never fails.

00:43:17.617 --> 00:43:21.883
Paris, did you program
this guy?

00:43:21.921 --> 00:43:23.286
Yeah. Why?

00:43:23.322 --> 00:43:25.756
He's a pig, and so are you.

00:43:32.065 --> 00:43:32.963
Almost never.

00:43:33.066 --> 00:43:35.227
Is this pool or billiards?

00:43:35.268 --> 00:43:37.429
Uh, pool.

00:43:37.470 --> 00:43:38.767
Right.

00:43:38.805 --> 00:43:40.238
Pool's the one with the pockets.

00:43:40.273 --> 00:43:42.673
Would you mind
if I gave it a try?

00:43:42.708 --> 00:43:44.869
Reculez-vous!

00:43:44.911 --> 00:43:47.106
Give the handsome
young woman some room.

00:43:48.314 --> 00:43:51.249
Tell me, does she
have, uh, money?

00:43:51.284 --> 00:43:53.844
Commander Chakotay, your stick?

00:43:53.886 --> 00:43:55.911
It's called a cue, Captain.

00:43:55.955 --> 00:43:57.286
Cue.

00:43:57.323 --> 00:43:58.790
All right.

00:43:58.825 --> 00:43:59.985
So what do we do?

00:44:00.059 --> 00:44:01.856
Do I go first?

00:44:13.406 --> 00:44:14.930
Solids.

00:44:14.974 --> 00:44:19.070
I saw that coming
a mile away, didn't you?

00:44:21.080 --> 00:44:24.948
Ah, you've got a lot
to learn, jeune homme.

00:44:25.017 --> 00:44:27.918
But then... I've got
a lot to teach.

00:44:29.255 --> 00:44:31.155
Eight ball in the side pocket.

00:44:32.391 --> 00:44:34.689
A-koo-chee-moya.

00:44:34.727 --> 00:44:36.388
We are far
from the sacred places

00:44:36.429 --> 00:44:39.421
of our grandfathers, and
from the bones of our people,

00:44:39.465 --> 00:44:41.558
but perhaps there is
one powerful being

00:44:41.601 --> 00:44:43.228
who will embrace this good crew

00:44:43.269 --> 00:44:45.362
and give them
the answer they seek.
